window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>I’m supposed to be the last of my kind, all-powerful, and marked by prophecy for greatness. But, something, somewhere, must have gone wrong, because I have <i>no</i> power or greatness. Just a flare for theft and a quick mouth that gets me in trouble. </p> <p>The prophecy must be about my sister, the only other living being with our kind's blood in her veins, but she's been in a magical sleep for eight years and is slowly turning to stone. </p> <p>I will do anything to save her, but the answers I need are inside Poseidon’s underwater palace.</p> <p>The fiercely powerful ocean god rules his realm with brutal efficiency, and nobody is ever allowed to get close to him. Some whisper about him being a monster. Unfortunately for me, I know his secret. </p> <p>In fact, I <i>am</i> his secret. </p> <p>I’m Poseidon’s secret bride, cast out of Aquarius and told never to return. </p> <p>I don’t recall our wedding vows saying anything about me obeying him, though, and I’ll do whatever it takes to save my sister—even risk the devastating ocean god’s deadly wrath. </p> <p><b><i>Secret of the Broken King </i></b><b>is the first book in the Poseidon Trials trilogy. Expect magic, mythology, and a searing slow-burn enemies-to-lovers romance that will leave you desperate for more. </b></p>"; 
